course: dictionary
lesson: 3807
title: Foreigner and the kind word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A foreigner is a person from another country. When you meet this word, look at the words around it for clues. «In Athens women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.» The sentence lists foreigners with women and slaves as people who were not allowed to vote, so you can tell the word names a group of people from outside.
explain: «Japan chose another path and from the 1630s shut its doors to most foreigners, letting only Dutch and Chinese traders in at Nagasaki.» Shutting doors and letting only some traders in shows that foreigners were people from other countries who were kept out. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: The word can sound unfriendly, so kind speakers often choose a gentler word. People might say «visitor» or «someone from abroad» instead. Some words are borderline: «lǎowài» (LAOW-WIGH) is a casual Chinese word for foreigner, and it is mostly harmless, but some people do not like being labelled that way.
fact: A foreigner is a person from another country.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «a foreigner in a strange land» and «treat foreigners kindly».
fact: «Lǎowài» (China) is a casual word for foreigner. It literally means "old outsider".
fact: Gentler words for foreigner include visitor and someone from abroad.
fact: When you read, check the context first: the sentence around the word often shows whether it is a group of people, a place, or a feeling.
exercise: «In Athens women, slaves and foreigners could not vote.» What is a foreigner? | *A person from another country | A ruler of the people | A person who is not allowed to vote in Athens | A slave who works in a house
exercise: «Japan... shut its doors to most foreigners, letting only Dutch and Chinese traders in.» What does shutting doors to foreigners suggest? | Only Japanese people had doors | The doors were painted in bright colours | *Most people from other countries were kept out | Everyone was welcomed with a party
exercise: Which word is a gentler choice than foreigner? | *Visitor | Outsider | Alien | Stranger
test: «Treat foreigners kindly.» What does this phrase ask us to do? | Ignore people from other countries | Make them pay more money | Send them home at once | *Be friendly and fair to people from other countries
test: Mei says «lǎowài» is a casual word for foreigner. What does the word literally mean? | Happy traveller | *Old outsider | A well-known friend | A young visitor
exam: «Some people don't like being labelled a foreigner, so a kind writer might choose visitor or someone from abroad.» Why would a writer choose a gentler word? | Because visitor means a person who must pay a fee | Because foreigner is always the most polite word | Because gentler words have no meaning at all | *Because foreigner can sound unfriendly to some people
